 R←Test_54(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;H;i;list;log;state;filename
⍝ `Process` with `stormGuard` 1: an occurrence the backoff would hold back gets the full treatment when the
⍝ last one is older than `stormRepeatAfter` hours, and the note in the log says so
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

⍝ Preconditions...
 #.⎕SHADOW'HandleErrorParms'
 #.HandleErrorParms←##.HandleError.CreateParms
 #.HandleErrorParms.killThreads←0                    ⍝ Killing threads would kill the session's own threads
 #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder←GetTempPath⊃⎕SI
 #.HandleErrorParms.saveErrorWS←0
 #.HandleErrorParms.stormGuard←1
 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP'
 'TEMP'#.⎕NS''
 #.TEMP.∆TheLog←''
 #.TEMP.⎕FX'{r}←∆CustomLogFns msg' '∆TheLog,←{1≥≡⍵:⊂⍵ ⋄ ⍵}msg'
 #.HandleErrorParms.logFunction←'#.TEMP.∆CustomLogFns'
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
 {}'CREATE!'FilesAndDirs.CheckPath #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
 H←##.HandleError
 filename←#.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder,'/StormGuard.txt'

 ⎕TRAP←(405 'E' '406 ##.HandleError.Process #.HandleErrorParms')(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 :For i :In ⍳2
     :Trap 406
         {⎕SIGNAL ⍵}405
         →T.GoToTidyUp 1
     :EndTrap
     :If 1=i                                          ⍝ Pretend it was occurrence 5, with the full treatment at 4, 25 hours ago
         state←H.ReadStormFile filename
         state.counts←,5
         state.lastFulls←,4
         state.lastFullTimes-←25×3600
         state.fulls←⍬
         filename H.WriteStormFile state
         #.TEMP.∆TheLog←''
     :EndIf
 :EndFor

 list←FilesAndDirs.ListFiles #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder,'/*.html'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2≠≢list                                ⍝ Occurrence 6 was not held back
 →T.GoToTidyUp 6≢#.HandleErrorParms.stormCount
 log←#.TEMP.∆TheLog
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/∨/¨'Storm guard: occurrence 6 '∘⍷¨log
 →T.GoToTidyUp∨/∨/¨'held back'∘⍷¨log
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/∨/¨'hours old'∘⍷¨log

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
